  "notes": "Cash-basis county, governmental funds only (no business-type funds). Statement receipts/disbursements from Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances, Total Governmental Funds column (p4). Taxes 3,081,203 split into property/motor vehicle/lodging using the Statement of Activities general receipts (p2); the three add to the printed total. Local 1,135,520 split the same way: charges for services 270,085 + interest income 139,457 + miscellaneous 725,978 (p2) = 1,135,520. Beginning/ending cash = fund balances (cash basis). Debt proceeds = bond + lease proceeds; other financing = bond premium (net) + sale of surplus. Transfers in and out each 1,046,372 (statement); General Fund budget schedule p8 shows transfers in 130,012/out 1,042,954 (General Fund sub-fund only; p5 total General Fund incl. Inheritance Tax and Veteran's Aid funds shows 131,606/1,167,954). General Fund detail uses the budgetary schedule p8 (General Fund column only, departmental lines); its function totals differ from the combining statement p5 column (e.g. general government 1,760,489 vs 1,698,208) but tie to its own printed total 3,522,335; the p5 combining General Fund total column is not duplicated, only the Inheritance Tax and Veteran's Aid funds are recorded from p5. Nonmajor funds have 10 columns, so Total column used (p7). Road fund detail disbursements are one line. Transfer cross-check: Road transfers in 1,041,360 matches General Fund transfers out 1,042,954 (+ Inheritance 125,000 out sends to other funds incl. General 130,012 in); no hidden transfers inside spending lines found; General Fund 'Miscellaneous' 1,073,419 flagged for review. The p4 statement and the p5 combining statement classify 172 differently in the Total General Fund column: general government 1,734,770 (p4) vs 1,734,598 (p5) and capital outlay 1,249,048 (p4) vs 1,249,220 (p5); total disbursements 4,615,625 agree, so no report discrepancy in totals; p4 figures used for the statement lines. Read pages 1-12 of 12"
